            "rawHtml": "<h3>THE LEGACY MODEL</h3><p class=\"lead-statement\">Perimeter Defense: The Castle-and-Moat Trusted</p><div class=\"info-card mt-3\"><p>Internal LAN INTERNET FIREWALL DMZ The old assumption: everything inside the network edge is safe. &quot;trust anyone inside the network&quot; A hardened outer boundary (firewalls, VPNs, gateways) separates &quot;trusted&quot; internal traffic from the &quot;untrusted&quot; internet. Once authenticated at the edge, users and devices are broadly trusted to roam the internal network. Security investment concentrates on keeping attackers out -- not on limiting what happens if they get in. 03 / 20</p></div>",
