            "lead": "THE NEW MODEL What Is Zero Trust Architecture? \"Never trust, always verify.\"",
            "isTitleSlide": false,
            "isSectionDivider": false,
            "rawHtml": "<h3>THE NEW MODEL</h3><p class=\"lead-statement\">What Is Zero Trust Architecture? &quot;Never trust, always verify.&quot;</p><div class=\"info-card mt-3\"><p>Zero Trust Architecture (ZTA) is a security model that assumes no user, device, or network segment -- inside or outside the organization -- should be trusted by default. Every request for access must be authenticated, authorized, and continuously validated. 05 / 20 Originated in 2011  with John Kindervag (former Forrester analyst)- he wrote the foundational Zero Trust papers. ✔ ZTA is a SECURITY STRATEGY , NOT A PRODUCT - eliminates the assumption of trust within a network ✔ ZTS (Zero Trust Security) -an IT model that demands strict identity checks for every person and device accessing a private network ✔ ZTNA (Zero Trust Network Access) - core technology linked to ZTA</p></div>",
            "cleanText": "THE NEW MODEL What Is Zero Trust Architecture? \"Never trust, always verify.\" Zero Trust Architecture (ZTA) is a security model that assumes no user, device, or network segment -- inside or outside the organization -- should be trusted by default. Every request for access must be authenticated, authorized, and continuously validated. 05 / 20 Originated in 2011  with John Kindervag (former Forrester analyst)- he wrote the foundational Zero Trust papers. ✔ ZTA is a SECURITY STRATEGY , NOT A PRODUCT - eliminates the assumption of trust within a network ✔ ZTS (Zero Trust Security) -an IT model that demands strict identity checks for every person and device accessing a private network ✔ ZTNA (Zero Trust Network Access) - core technology linked to ZTA",
