            "rawHtml": "<h3>THE NEW MODEL</h3><p class=\"lead-statement\">What Is Zero Trust Architecture? 05 / 20</p><div class=\"info-card mt-3\"><p>EXAMPLE SCENARIO An engineer at a software company requests access to the production database from the office. Even though she is on the corporate network, Zero Trust still verifies her identity with MFA, checks that her laptop meets security policy, confirms she is a member of the database-access group, and grants only read access to the specific schema she needs 1 Identity verified → 2 Device checked → 3 Context evaluated → 4 Least-priv. access granted Verification happens for every single request -- not once at the door.</p></div><ul class=\"compact mt-3\"><li>re-checking all of this on her next request.</li></ul>",
