            "subtitle": "Core Principles of Zero Trust (NIST SP 800-207)",
            "lead": "CORE PRINCIPLE 02 Least-Privilege Access MINIMUM",
            "isTitleSlide": false,
            "isSectionDivider": false,
            "rawHtml": "<h3>CORE PRINCIPLE 02</h3><p class=\"lead-statement\">Least-Privilege Access MINIMUM</p><div class=\"info-card mt-3\"><p>Just enough access, just in time. Users, apps, and services get only the permissions required for their specific task -- nothing broader, and often only for a limited time window. Broad access &quot;All employees can read the entire shared drive, including HR and finance folders, in case they ever need to.&quot; Least privilege &quot;Each employee sees only their own team&#x27;s folder; HR data is granted per-request, per-case, and expires automatically.&quot; 07 / 20</p></div>",
            "cleanText": "CORE PRINCIPLE 02 Least-Privilege Access MINIMUM Just enough access, just in time. Users, apps, and services get only the permissions required for their specific task -- nothing broader, and often only for a limited time window. Broad access \"All employees can read the entire shared drive, including HR and finance folders, in case they ever need to.\" Least privilege \"Each employee sees only their own team's folder; HR data is granted per-request, per-case, and expires automatically.\" 07 / 20",
