            "isTitleSlide": false,
            "isSectionDivider": false,
            "rawHtml": "<h3>CORE PRINCIPLE 02</h3><p class=\"lead-statement\">Least-Privilege Access MINIMUM</p><div class=\"info-card mt-3\"><p>Just enough access, just in time. Users, apps, and services get only the permissions required for their specific task -- nothing broader, and often only for a limited time window. EXAMPLE SCENARIO A third-party contractor is hired to fix one bug in a billing microservice. Under least privilege, the access system grants a scoped, time-boxed credential to just that service&#x27;s staging environment for 48 hours -- not the full production network. When the contract ends, access expires automatically instead of lingering as an unused, exploitable account. 07 / 20</p></div>",
            "cleanText": "CORE PRINCIPLE 02 Least-Privilege Access MINIMUM Just enough access, just in time. Users, apps, and services get only the permissions required for their specific task -- nothing broader, and often only for a limited time window. EXAMPLE SCENARIO A third-party contractor is hired to fix one bug in a billing microservice. Under least privilege, the access system grants a scoped, time-boxed credential to just that service's staging environment for 48 hours -- not the full production network. When the contract ends, access expires automatically instead of lingering as an unused, exploitable account. 07 / 20",
