            "isTitleSlide": false,
            "isSectionDivider": false,
            "rawHtml": "<h3>CORE PRINCIPLE 04</h3><p class=\"lead-statement\">Microsegmentation Instead of one flat internal network, Zero Trust</p><div class=\"info-card mt-3\"><p>divides infrastructure into small, isolated zones -- each with its own access controls. Contains attackers to a single segment Enforces policy between workloads, not just at the edge Makes lateral movement visible and blockable 09 / 20</p></div>",
            "cleanText": "CORE PRINCIPLE 04 Microsegmentation Instead of one flat internal network, Zero Trust divides infrastructure into small, isolated zones -- each with its own access controls. Contains attackers to a single segment Enforces policy between workloads, not just at the edge Makes lateral movement visible and blockable 09 / 20",
