            "eyebrow": "CIT 220 • Unit 02.1",
            "subtitle": "Continuous Monitoring, Analytics & Implementation",
            "lead": "SIDE BY SIDE Zero Trust vs. Perimeter Defense PERIMETER DEFENSE ZERO TRUST",
            "isTitleSlide": false,
            "isSectionDivider": false,
            "rawHtml": "<h3>SIDE BY SIDE</h3><p class=\"lead-statement\">Zero Trust vs. Perimeter Defense PERIMETER DEFENSE ZERO TRUST</p><div class=\"info-card mt-3\"><p>Trust model Trusted inside, untrusted outside Never trust; verify every request Access scope Broad access once inside the network Least privilege, scoped per resource Verification One-time, at login or network entry Continuous, re-checked per request Breach impact Attacker can move laterally, unchecked Blast radius contained by segmentation Best fit for Fixed offices, on-prem-only networks Cloud, remote work, hybrid environments EXAMPLE SCENARIO Google&#x27;s internal BeyondCorp initiative replaced VPN-based perimeter access with per-request, identity- and device-aware verification for every employee application -- a widely cited real-world case of the shift this table describes. 16 / 20</p></div>",
            "cleanText": "SIDE BY SIDE Zero Trust vs. Perimeter Defense PERIMETER DEFENSE ZERO TRUST Trust model Trusted inside, untrusted outside Never trust; verify every request Access scope Broad access once inside the network Least privilege, scoped per resource Verification One-time, at login or network entry Continuous, re-checked per request Breach impact Attacker can move laterally, unchecked Blast radius contained by segmentation Best fit for Fixed offices, on-prem-only networks Cloud, remote work, hybrid environments EXAMPLE SCENARIO Google's internal BeyondCorp initiative replaced VPN-based perimeter access with per-request, identity- and device-aware verification for every employee application -- a widely cited real-world case of the shift this table describes. 16 / 20",
            "codeSnippets": [],
