            "eyebrow": "CIT 220 • Unit 02.1",
            "subtitle": "Landmark Case Studies: SolarWinds & MS Exchange",
            "lead": "Microsoft Exchange Hack (2021) What Happened: Attackers exploited vulnerabilities in Microsoft Exchange's email",
            "isTitleSlide": false,
            "isSectionDivider": false,
            "rawHtml": "<h3>Microsoft Exchange Hack (2021)</h3><p class=\"lead-statement\">What Happened: Attackers exploited vulnerabilities in Microsoft Exchange&#x27;s email</p><div class=\"info-card mt-3\"><p>servers, bypassing insufficient access controls to compromise sensitive data and leaked some of the data information. Implications: Highlighted the need for robust identity verification and continuous monitoring to detect unusual behavior. Meta&#x27;s Internal Tool Breach (2022) What Happened: Phishing attacks granted hackers access to Meta&#x27;s internal tools, underscoring the risks of inadequate device authentication. Implications: Reinforced the importance of endpoint security in Zero Trust frameworks. The Cost of Failure: Case Studies of ZTA Breaches</p></div>",
