            "isTitleSlide": false,
            "isSectionDivider": false,
            "rawHtml": "<h3>SUMMARY</h3><p class=\"lead-statement\">Key Takeaways 1 The network perimeter no longer defines the security boundary -- identity, device, and</p><div class=\"info-card mt-3\"><p>context do. 2 &quot;Never trust, always verify&quot; means continuous, per-request verification -- not a one-time login check. 3 Least privilege and microsegmentation shrink the blast radius when -- not if -- a breach occurs. 4 Zero Trust is a phased journey across identity, devices, network, apps, and data -- not a single product. The goal isn&#x27;t a perfect, unbreachable network -- it&#x27;s a network where a single stolen password or infected laptop never becomes a full-scale breach. 19 / 20</p></div>",
